  "title": "Amazon Toddler Step Stool Recall: Thousands of Children’s Towers Pulled Over Serious Safety Risks",
  "summary": "Parents and caregivers are being urged to stop using certain toddler step stools sold through Amazon after safety officials announced recalls involving more than 130,000 units. The recalled products have been linked to fall, tipping, and entrapment risks that could lead to serious injuries or, in extreme cases, death. The recalls involve two popular children’s tower stool brands: Woodure children’s tower kitchen step stools and HARPPA Nordi foldable toddler towers. According to the U.S. Consume",
